.TH INPUTWEAVE-APP 1 "2026-10-29" "InputWeave" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inputweave-app \- the InputWeave app
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B inputweave-app
.RB [ \-\-background ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The InputWeave app shows the background service's state and settings: the
arrangement of the computers, pairing, file transfers and troubleshooting.
It puts an icon in the panel's status area where the desktop shows one
(KDE Plasma; GNOME with the AppIndicator extension, which Ubuntu turns on).
Started from the application menu it opens its window; the first time, it
walks through setting up.
.PP
Closing the window leaves the app in the status area; sharing goes on in
the background service (\fBinputweave\fR(1)) whether the app runs or not.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-background
Put up only the status icon, as when opened at login.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR inputweave (1)
